  "published": "2026-11-26T19:30:07.777Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Version 0.11.0\n\nTargets .NET 11.\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n*   **Target framework**: Requires .NET 11.\n*   **Unique context options**: `NpgsqlDbContextOptionsAttribute`, `NpgsqlPerformanceSettingsAttribute`, `DrnContextDefaultsAttribute`, and `DrnContextPerformanceDefaultsAttribute` now use `AllowMultiple = false`. Derived-context declarations replace inherited ones of the same type, and multiple instances of the same options attribute type throw `ConfigurationException`.\n*   **Sealed defaults attributes**: `DrnContextDefaultsAttribute` and `DrnContextPerformanceDefaultsAttribute` are now sealed. Derive custom attributes from `NpgsqlDbContextOptionsAttribute` or `NpgsqlPerformanceSettingsAttribute` instead.\n*   **Transitive analyzers**: SharedKernel classification errors (`DRNCLASSIFICATION*`) and application convention warnings (`DRNPERSISTENCE007`/`008`/`009`, `DRNSTRUCTURE006`/`007`, `DRNREPOSITORY004`, `DRNOWNERSHIP003`) apply transitively. Concrete `DrnContext` classes must directly apply a custom `NpgsqlDbContextOptionsAttribute` descendant (`<ContextName>*Options[Attribute]`), expose `AggregateRoot` `DbSet` properties, use `Repositories`, `Configurations` (`*Config`), and `Migrations` folders, implement `IDrnContext`, and pair assigned aggregates with concrete `SourceKnownRepository` implementations.\n\n### New Features\n\n*   **Convention persistence metadata**: Added `SourceKnownPersistenceAttribute` to record context and entity inclusion or exclusion for convention analysis without changing the EF model.\n\n---\n\nDocumented with the assistance of [DiSC OS](https://github.com/duranserkan/DRN-Project/blob/develop/.agent/rules/DiSCOS.md)\n\n---\n**Semper Progressivus: Always Progressive**",
